## Chains of thought becoming obsolete

Recurrent architectures might just be better. It would be a stunning coincidence
if the most observable way to get reasoning out of models is also the most performant.
Note that most human thinking is not even done in English - some people do not have
inner monologues and are clearly capable of reasoning. That is not actually proof that
their reasoning doesn't happen in English just unconsciously, but humans who do not
have language are still capable of reasoning to some extent.

Even if they are not actually better, they may be more computationally efficient.

